00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.720
MILLION COLOR!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.180
TURNS!

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.650
<i>The Asteroid Colony, Mistletoe. It was an agricultural colony...</i>

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.940
<i>...constructed by Queen Dianna's ancestors to produce large quantities of food for the moon.</i>

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.120
<i>It was there we were separated from the Willgem...</i>

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:43.410
<i>But Mistletoe was then ransacked and wrecked by the Mahiroo Squad.</i>

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.630
<b>The Asteroid's Explosion</b>

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.950
The White Doll and Kapool have been located.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.450
- Can we reach them?
- Yes.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.240
Militia soldiers, watch the enemy team's movements closely.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.410
Captain Michael, get our machine-guns manned.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.410
Everyone, prepare for surface to air combat!

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.210
It's no good!

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.630
Is the Kapool there?

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.710
I can't get a reading with all of these rocks in the way...

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.920
I'm clearing the debris from the data.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.800
Apart from the Mustache, there are 4 of them, right?

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.720
It looks like the Willgem made it out.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.520
Did you all see that?

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.730
Roger. They should be able to detect us soon.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.520
But the enemy's probably going to lock onto us soon as well.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.320
Wouldn't they have already done so by now?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.320
With Queen Dianna here...

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.320
And I think I can use this mobile suit now.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.410
Withdraw.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.540
All forces are to withdraw from the colony's remains.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.420
What do you think you're doing? Resume your formation!

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.420
Roger!

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.020
Locate that shuttle!

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.310
Sir! We're locating the shuttle now.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.020
Sweatson understands what comes next after we've completed E-Minor, correct?

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.030
They're in the process of deploying the Ursa Major formation.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.410
Did you really manage to escape Mistletoe?

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:55.330
I suppose it's to be expected, or there'd be no reason to use Ursa Major!

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.710
So, Harry Ord...

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:01.130
I wonder how Dianna will react to Mistletoe ending up like this.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.220
Dianna should only ever be addressed by her title of "Queen".

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.850
That makes me wonder just what's on your mind, General.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.220
Oops... A simple slip of the tongue.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:14.150
The only thing on my mind was keeping my men's morale focused.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.730
Do you read me, Queen Dianna?

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.610
Yes. What is it, Loran?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.410
Are you alright with piloting that shuttle?

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:31.040
It's fine. Miss Kihel is the one whom I'm worried about.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.420
Harry has probably taken her to Ghingnham.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.330
Then he must have made contact with that ship.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.220
Lady Sochie, please don't head out on your own!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.640
And where do you plan to go?

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.230
That place is where my sister currently is! Didn't Miss Dianna just say so!?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:57.230
Mr. Harry is using Kihel as a body double for Queen Dianna.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.110
You mustn't worry about her.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.610
But we can't guarantee she'll make it out alive. This is still a war.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.120
Stand back, Little lady.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.040
It's best to leave the job up to a machine of the same type!

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.330
See that? You can depend on me!

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.210
Queen Dianna has given me all of her strength.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.920
That's the Moonrace for you.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.010
Ms. Cancer...

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.510
Her strength is even greater here than on earth...

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.510
Trigger!

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.930
A direct hit...

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.730
How unforeseen.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.230
The data tells me that shot should've missed.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.610
It seems that real combat differs from a simulation.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.110
I don't understand!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.610
The first wave has been destroyed...!?

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.820
The enemy can't just cut through that easily, can they?

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.910
Have Midgard assist us in recording our enemy's tactics.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.540
The Willgem seems to have escaped as well!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.340
To anyone without a space suit...

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.340
Please remain near the life-pods or wine barrels to prepare for any emergency we may encounter.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:13.140
Let's see...Everyone else... envision this as if it were a battle on the Atlantic in the 1640s.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.520
What's this? A battle on the Atlantic?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.730
In old naval battles, ships could only fire on one another at a distance of about 100 meters.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.650
But this is a space battle...

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:24.320
I know that... Just keep firing warning shots and avoid destroying the enemy ship.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.820
I'm not skilled enough to pull that off...!

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.530
But isn't Queen Dianna in that one?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.620
Spread the fire out by 30 percent!

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:39.710
Now I understand!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:42.130
Despite having locked on them, we still can't hit them...

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.710
Targeting a ship is different from targeting debris!

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:50.930
If you're still treating war like a training simulation, you'll never learn to adapt to the real thing.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.010
The colony's debris will be our shield!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:07.610
If the enemy wishes to contact us, let them. Whatever they have to say, we should hear them out.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.030
What do you intend to accomplish out here in space, Militia?

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.740
I'm not sure what you're talking about.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:17.410
Is trapping people and overwhelming them with firepower typical behavior in the Moonrace?

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.540
How is that not barbaric?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.540
We simply intended to recapture the shuttle that'd fled the Gendarme.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:28.630
Regardless of the reason behind it, aggressive treatment towards those who have come for negotiations...

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.220
...must also be considered savage!

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.130
Wartime negotiations?

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:36.140
That's the reason we've placed our lives in danger and flown to space!

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.720
I intend to speak with your leaders!

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.810
Those are bold words...

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:44.230
It also seems as though we both intend...

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:45.440
...to recapture those who have fled from us.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.520
Recapture?

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.730
Fled?

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:52.740
It's not that. Sir Guin is indirectly giving us an order to move as we please.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:56.740
Really, now? That man is a fast talker.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.910
Inform Agrippa.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.410
There will be plenty of opportunities to battle them in the future.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.630
For now, we'll allow them to negotiate.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.420
Leave the second fleet to its own devices.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.140
If this continues, they'll sneak into our cannon's blind spot!

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.810
We'll circle around it!

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.310
The debris is currently accelerating due to the Moon's gravity!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.230
It's on a direct course for Von city!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.120
Cancer!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:42.330
Please forgive me for having left you to pilot the shuttle alone.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.710
Don't worry about it. Let's just proceed straight to the moon.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.710
Straight? The debris is heading directly for the moon!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.840
Correct. It will most likely be a direct hit.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.130
My family line was the one who built Mistletoe...

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.220
...and now it's going to destroy Von City.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.640
Von City? There's where the House of Kafka originated!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.140
Is that so?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.440
Then you can depend on me!

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:09.110
As the descendents of the Kafka family, the Red Team must prevent this from occurring, no matter the cost!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.820
What can you do in a Mahiroo?

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:11.940
I'll do what I can!

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.110
Cancer!

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.610
What do you mean!?

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.820
How can a colony collide with the Moon?

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:20.620
It was being balanced between the gravities of both the Earth and the Moon...

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.540
But the explosion knocked it out of its orbit, and now it's being pulled in by the moon's gravity.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.120
You mean it's going to fall on the moon!?

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.420
Yes. That's correct.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.630
Why?

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.210
I already explained it to you!

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.340
What? You're kidding!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.630
I explained it!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.130
How is that?

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.430
Von city has a population of 200,000...

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.720
Not counting the people living around its vicinity.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.510
Gather the remaining units around the Aspite.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.730
The second fleet is to remain on course.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.810
Mistletoe's debris is going to collide with Von City.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:54.740
Mistletoe? Von City!?

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.410
The people will have no time to evacuate.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:02.530
Send any available ships to assist them!

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:05.540
Is there a way to destroy Mistletoe?

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.920
We lack a weapon with that firepower.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:14.210
Even if we fired every Mega Particle Cannon at once, there'd be no way to destroy the entire thing.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.510
How dare you!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.720
You're saying you don't care about saving Von city!?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.930
Sounding an alarm would only result in a panic.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.810
There is currently no time for an evacuation.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.520
And you call yourself one of the Moonrace!?

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:31.020
You now have gained my interest... Dianna Soriel, you say?

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.940
When I touch your hair, it still feels the same.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.530
And if it turns out I am not Dianna, what then?

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:47.540
Then it'd mean that at one point, Dianna Counter was under the leadership of a mere earth woman!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:53.130
As a leader, I'd be just as interested in such a woman.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:57.210
Both as a commanding woman... and as a lady.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.010
...I will strike you if I must!

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:06.720
Excellent! Please do! I invite you to freely do so!

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.640
Please stop this!

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:12.730
What is the meaning of this!?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.820
The princess was simply admiring my katana.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.020
Your katana?

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:19.030
It seems to be suited to her tastes.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.530
Sir Ghingnham...

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.620
It would seem Gym Ghingnham is quite the martial arts master.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.330
Master?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.700
I'll go seek out a solution for this Von City crisis.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.760
Ready the X Top!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.890
Be sure the X Top is prepared!

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:48.560
What are your intentions? The colony debris will...

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.270
That's why I intend to use the X Top.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.480
X Top?

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:57.480
What? It's the perfect device for taking control of the Keilas Guilie system.

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.280
You intend to use Keilas Guilie?

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.280
Precisely.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.950
It's the only thing that can reduce the debris to space dust.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:09.950
After all, I've now made a promise to Queen Dianna Soriel.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:14.250
Bastard...

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.760
These bastards are determined to kill Queen Dianna...

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.180
But I'll stop them!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:25.890
Hold off, Sis, don't go overboard!

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.180
Move it!

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:31.480
If we can take their battleship, we ram it into the debris and possibly prevent it from hitting the moon!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.850
It won't work!

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.360
Otherwise, we could try using the Militia's spacecraft!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.150
Please tell me you're not serious!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:44.780
Even if it's next to impossible, I cannot allow our Queen to suffer more grief!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:50.870
Her ancestors built Mistletoe, and now it's going to destroy one of the moon's cities!

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.080
I'm going!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.370
What are you doing!?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.670
I'll melt it.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:56.960
What are you going to do?

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:00.170
I'll use the nuclear bombs the White Doll's been carrying.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.260
Nuclear bombs!?

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.970
Why did you bring a thing like that!?

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.970
I've been safe-guarding them... ever since Lost Mountain.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.550
I'll put them to good use.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:14.060
Second Team, are you finished playing yet!?

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:16.980
We'll now move in on them using the cyclone formation!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:20.860
Are we beaten?

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:24.490
Milady, accompany the Red Team and escape in that shuttle.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.490
Use the Lance formation!

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:29.070
You should know what to do next. Understood?

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.750
We'll hold back the Mobile Suits.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:43.670
Oh right! Little lady, please take Her Majesty Dianna and escape from this battlefield!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:44.880
I understand.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.550
Loran, you can do it, right?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.180
You can count on me, Milady.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.550
Miss Laura of the Mustache...

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.270
I don't care whether you're Loran or Laura anymore!

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:57.850
I now see that you're a true person of the Moonrace, full of love for our Queen.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.860
We'll leave the rest up to you! Muron!

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.150
Sis!

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:05.570
Miss Cancer, Mr. Muron, I'm going to blow it up before it hits the moon.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.650
Try and get to the other side to avoid the explosion!

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:08.780
After we beat these bastards!

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.370
Is this really alright?

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:14.450
It's time now. Make your way closer to the moon to avoid the blast.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:15.870
Loran, it's up to you.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:16.790
Right.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.250
Please use the bomb to insure that those on the moon are safe.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.460
Of course.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:22.880
And keep yourself safe.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.880
Queen Dianna... everyone will be saved.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.180
That's the Turn X Top...

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:37.560
So it can be used as the Keilas Guilie control system?

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.190
Can you keep up, SUMO?

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.650
I can attempt to.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.480
So we've learned some modesty, have we?

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.860
Excellent.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.370
So what can this machine do?

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.670
What in the...!?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.550
Should I throw the Nukes...?

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.970
I've got two Nukes.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:22.060
I wish I had more time to practice in this machine...

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:27.860
You're not bad!

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:37.870
Looks like someone left the colony wreckage.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.460
They appear the be Mobile Suits. Harry, do you know who it could be?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.580
The one with the Mustache is called the "White Doll".

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:46.250
It's a unique suit that walked out of a statue called the "White Doll".

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.460
And that means what?

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.760
Exactly what I just told you.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.470
It doesn't appear that he's preparing to attack us at the moment.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.970
Then what do you think he's currently trying to do?

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.270
The Mustache's pilot is from the earth.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.180
Space can be terrifying. He's probably just flying around at random.

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.150
Should be in range...

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.860
People of the Moonrace, listen to me!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:16.070
The White Doll now possesses a great sword, once sealed in the Dark History, which can burn the heavens!

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:19.450
In order to prevent Mistletoe's debris from striking the moon...

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.450
I am now preparing to draw this sword!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:28.460
Everyone who's in this vicinity must now leave. You don't want to be enveloped by the weapon's heat and radiation!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:31.880
What is he talking about!?

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.550
The nuclear bombs from Lost Mountain!

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:38.470
Has the Mustache been keeping those ever since that day!?

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.770
Damn that Loran... to think that he'd plan something like this...

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.690
That man...

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:47.190
Does he intend to reach the moon with nuclear bombs still in hand?

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:51.990
Such a weapon shouldn't be used, should it... Sir Guin?

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:56.570
It's better than letting the debris strike the moon! We'd better listen to Loran!

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.450
Understood. Pull back!

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:01.290
I'll leave our course to you, Jacop, Bruno!

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.290
Roger!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.370
Willgem, fly as far from the Mustache as possible.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.250
Roger.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.580
I've picked up a Kapool.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.670
Just a Kapool?

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:10.250
No, there's a shuttle with it.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.880
Keep monitoring the surroundings.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.550
The White Doll's pilot means what he said!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.470
The light we witnessed from Lost Mountain was another nuclear bomb!

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:25.690
Gym Ghingnham, cease your battle formations. Recall your forces now!

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.780
Loran... I never realized that he had a nuclear weapon with him.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:36.570
A Dianna Counter officer entrusted them to him for disposal.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.450
But he never have the chance to do so yet.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.870
Is that how it is? And he's been holding them until now...

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.460
Loran Cehack... is quite an interesting child.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.880
That light...

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:50.090
Zoom in.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.170
The Gold Type and another...

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:55.170
What's this? They'll be killed in the nuclear explosion!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.970
What's this cross shaped mark?

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.970
It's reacting, dear brother!

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:03.680
Brother?

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:07.690
If you're reacting with the "Turn X"... Then that makes you the "Turn A", Brother.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.860
The House of Ghingnham that built Genganam...

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:13.150
...now wishes for the Turn A to meet with them!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.150
Ghingnham...

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.990
I can see that you have Lieutenant Harry with you.

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:19.950
What are you going to do with Queen Dianna?

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:24.370
She has been brought aboard our ship, where she's treated as our honored leader.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.950
Is that the truth?

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:28.750
And what would you do if it weren't, Turn A?

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.960
If that's the case...

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.670
I have two of these heaven burning swords.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:38.970
If need be, I can spare one of them for your clan, Ghingnham!

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.760
Then in that case, you may do what you feel you must.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.470
I'll swear on that by my name, and by the Turn X!

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.190
Then I'll trust your word for now.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.650
If these are the products of human intellect...

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:55.150
...then work for the benefit of humanity!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.580
He did it!

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:12.960
Sis!

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.170
Everyone, I've launched the nukes!

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.180
I'm blowing them up now!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:32.690
Did I miss? Where's the explosion?

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.870
What is this barrier!?

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.170
That damned Loran actually set off two Nuclear bombs!

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.250
What is this...!?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.670
Sis!

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.170
Can our machines endure this?

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.470
That's...

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.390
...the light from Lost Mountain!

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:09.680
It's the light of dawn in Space...

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.350
Gavane... Gavane Gooney...

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.780
All hands, make preparations to clear out the debris from the explosion.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.360
The Mega Particle Cannons are ready to fire the spread-shots!

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:26.950
Once we've cleaned out the remaining debris, the Mahiroo Team will retreat.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.790
You okay, Miss Dianna?

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:32.160
Yes... but I've lost track of Mr. Mustache's trace code...

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.370
It should be somewhere within in this area.

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:36.670
No way... Loran!?

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:41.170
I can't lose another person to that explosion...

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.670
It's the White Doll!

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:45.890
Yes, I've confirmed that here as well.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:47.180
Let's catch up with it!

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.470
Right!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.180
Cancer and Muron...

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:53.180
...there's no way I'll be able to track their location through all that debris.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.190
Where are the Willgem and Aspite?

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.490
The sound of the ringing bells has ceased.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:21.380
- Thanks!
- No biggie!

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.880
It feels great to be in such a wide space again.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:27.680
And how!

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:31.560
With this much space, you and I should be fine here for the next four or five days!

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.350
Do you have the food? Where's the Sake and dumplings?

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.560
Without these, we wouldn't be worthy of the name "Red Team", right?

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.190
Yahoo! Pass it over here!

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.070
You got it!

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:44.650
To celebrate Queen Dianna Soriel's return to the moon...

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.780
...I'll drink to your honor, Highness!

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:44.270
<i>I've now found myself by the moon's riverside, at my former home,</i>

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:47.940
<i>...all for the sake of taking Dianna back to the capital, Genganam.</i>

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:51.860
<i>A few of my old friends offer us assistance, but...</i>

00:23:51.860 --> 00:23:56.530
<i>...Ghingnham's Mobile Suit troops soon discovered us, and we're forced to engage them in an underwater battle.</i>

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.460
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:02.460
<i>Sea Battle On The Lunar Surface</i>

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:06.460
"The wind crosses over the canal."

00:24:03.620 --> 00:24:08.460
<b>Sea Battle On The Lunar Surface</b>
